# ── Phase 4a: observability + backups (docs/ops/BACKUP-RESTORE.md) ──────────
# Structured JSON logs: debug | info | warn | error (default info).
# LOG_LEVEL=info
# Build commit shown by GET /api/health and on error reports (compose passes
# it as a build arg: MARKETR_GIT_COMMIT=$(git rev-parse --short HEAD)).
# MARKETR_GIT_COMMIT=
# Sentry (or GlitchTip) error reporting — off unless the DSN is set.
# SENTRY_DSN=https://publickey@o0.ingest.sentry.io/0
# SENTRY_ENVIRONMENT=production
# SENTRY_RELEASE=
# OpenTelemetry tracing via @vercel/otel — off unless the endpoint is set.
# The exporter also reads the standard OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_HEADERS /
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_PROTOCOL / OTEL_RESOURCE_ATTRIBUTES variables.
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:4318
# OTEL_SERVICE_NAME=shapesos
# OTEL_SDK_DISABLED=
# Database backups (compose `backup` service / scripts/ops/backup.sh).
# BACKUP_DATABASE_URL=   (defaults to DATABASE_URL; must be the schema owner)
# BACKUP_DIR=./backups
# BACKUP_RETENTION_DAYS=14
# BACKUP_INTERVAL_SECONDS=86400
# BACKUP_S3_BUCKET=
# BACKUP_S3_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:9000
# BACKUP_S3_REGION=us-east-1
# BACKUP_S3_PREFIX=backups/
# BACKUP_S3_ACCESS_KEY=
# BACKUP_S3_SECRET_KEY=
# --- Phase 4a: identity (2FA, passkeys, SCIM, login step-up) ---
# Two-factor (TOTP) secrets are sealed with MARKETR_CREDENTIALS_KEY (above);
# set it before members enable an authenticator app.
# Passkeys (WebAuthn) take their relying-party ID and origin from APP_URL,
# then AUTH_URL, then NEXTAUTH_URL. In production one of them MUST be the
# public https URL users sign in on, or passkeys stay unavailable.
#AUTH_URL="https://app.example.com"
# CAPTCHA step-up after repeated failed password sign-ins (optional). With no
# provider (or an incomplete config) sign-in keeps the existing capped backoff
# only. CAPTCHA_PROVIDER is "turnstile" (Cloudflare) or "hcaptcha".
#CAPTCHA_PROVIDER="turnstile"
#CAPTCHA_SITE_KEY=""
#CAPTCHA_SECRET_KEY=""
# Failed attempts (per account or per IP, in the lockout window) before a
# CAPTCHA is required. Default 3; the lockout itself starts at 5 per account.
#LOGIN_CAPTCHA_AFTER_FAILURES="3"
# SCIM 2.0 needs no env: owners create per-workspace tokens in
# Settings → Security; the base URL is <APP_URL>/api/scim/v2.

# --- Phase 4b: live connector wiring (GA4, GSC, Google Ads, Meta Ads, Drive,
# Notion, Google Business Profile). Connections use the OAuth vault
# (GOOGLE_OAUTH_*, META_OAUTH_*, NOTION_OAUTH_*); without a stored credential
# every adapter stays in labeled mock mode.
# Google Ads developer token (API Center of the manager account); sent as the
# developer-token header. A BYO developerToken in the credential overrides it.
#GOOGLE_ADS_DEVELOPER_TOKEN=<redacted>
# Optional API version pins (defaults: v25 / v26.0, verified 2026-10).
#GOOGLE_ADS_API_VERSION="v25"
#META_GRAPH_API_VERSION="v26.0"
# Meta app credentials for the meta-ads OAuth flow; the secret also signs
# appsecret_proof on every Graph call.
#META_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=""
#META_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=<redacted>

# --- Phase 4b: mobile push notifications (Expo) ---
# The mobile app registers its Expo push token with /api/mobile/push-devices.
# Pushes (approval needed / decided, run failed) are sent only when
# PUSH_PROVIDER="expo"; unset = registration works, nothing is sent.
#PUSH_PROVIDER="expo"
# Only needed when "enhanced push security" is on for the Expo project.
#EXPO_ACCESS_TOKEN=""
# --- Phase 4b: inbound email replies (CRM conversation inbox) ---
# When set, outbound email carries a per-workspace Reply-To address
# (reply+<workspace>-<hmac>@<domain>). Point the domain's MX at Resend Inbound
# and add a Resend webhook for email.received → <APP_URL>/api/messaging/inbound/email.
# Replies are fetched with RESEND_API_KEY and threaded on the sender's lead.
#MESSAGING_INBOUND_EMAIL_DOMAIN="reply.example.com"
# Signs the reply addresses (required in production once the domain is set).
#MESSAGING_INBOUND_EMAIL_SECRET=""
# The signing secret of that Resend webhook (whsec_…). Unset = the endpoint answers 503.
#RESEND_INBOUND_WEBHOOK_SECRET=""
# Phase 4b social loop. Without POSTIZ_URL/POSTIZ_API_KEY, Social runs in
# sample mode outside production (sample channels, simulated publishing,
# sample engagement, all labelled). In production it shows "connect Postiz"
# instead, unless SOCIAL_MOCK_MODE=1 (demo instances only).
#SOCIAL_MOCK_MODE="0"
# Per-file cap for social media uploads, in MB (default 9.5). Uploads pass
# through proxy.ts, which buffers at most Next's proxyClientMaxBodySize
# (10 MB default); raise both together.
#SOCIAL_MAX_UPLOAD_MB="9.5"
# --- Phase 8 (ship): GitHub App mode for agent branches and pull requests ---
# When both are set, git_clone / git_push_branch / open_pull_request act as
# this GitHub App: an RS256 app JWT (iss = the app id) is exchanged for a
# short-lived installation token per repository (cached until expiry). Repos
# the app is not installed on fall back to a GitHub site's personal access
# token in the same workspace (Websites → GitHub). Unset = PAT mode only.
#GITHUB_APP_ID=""
# PEM private key of the app (PKCS#1 or PKCS#8); "\n" escapes are accepted.
#GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY=""
# --- Phase 9 (repos): continue agent pull requests from GitHub feedback ---
# Secret of the GitHub webhook pointed at https://<app>/api/hooks/github
# (content type application/json; events: pull request reviews, review
# comments, issue comments, check suites / runs, pull requests). Review
# feedback from repository collaborators on a shapes/<run id> branch sends the
# agent back to work in the same chat thread. Unset = the endpoint answers 503.
#GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET=""
# Webhook fallback (e.g. personal-access-token repos without a webhook): poll
# open agent PRs for new reviews, comments and failing checks every 5 minutes
# (cron job github-prs). on | off (default off).
#GITHUB_PR_POLL="off"

# --- Phase 8: code sandbox (agent code tools: read/write/edit files, bash, tests) ---
# One isolated sandbox per agent run, destroyed when the run ends, is stopped
# or idles out. Nothing runs on the app host. Without a reachable provider
# the code tools stay off and say why (Settings → Providers shows the status).
# docker (default) | e2b | daytona | off
#SANDBOX_PROVIDER="docker"
# Docker Engine API socket (mount it into the worker only). tcp:// is refused.
#DOCKER_HOST="unix:///var/run/docker.sock"
# Image for Docker sandboxes. Default: node:24.21.0-bookworm pinned by digest
# (node, npm, git, python3; non-root user `node`, uid 1000, home /home/node).
#SANDBOX_IMAGE=""
#SANDBOX_CPUS="2"
#SANDBOX_MEMORY_MB="2048"
#SANDBOX_PIDS="512"
# Docker: caps the workdir with a tmpfs-backed volume of this size (memory-
# backed). Unset = no hard disk cap (plain volumes can't be capped without
# xfs project quotas).
#SANDBOX_DISK_MB=""
#SANDBOX_IDLE_MINUTES="30"
# Extra hosts the sandbox may reach (comma-separated; package registries and
# GitHub are always allowed). Everything else is refused.
#SANDBOX_EGRESS_ALLOW=""
# Docker previews: the gateway publishes on SANDBOX_PREVIEW_BIND (Docker
# host) and the app reaches it at SANDBOX_PREVIEW_HOST.
#SANDBOX_PREVIEW_BIND="127.0.0.1"
#SANDBOX_PREVIEW_HOST="127.0.0.1"
# Docker checkpoints (tar of the workdir) — deleted with the sandbox.
#SANDBOX_SNAPSHOT_DIR=".data/sandbox-snapshots"
#SANDBOX_SNAPSHOT_MAX_MB="1024"
# E2B (SANDBOX_PROVIDER=e2b)
#E2B_API_KEY=""
#E2B_DOMAIN="e2b.app"
#E2B_TEMPLATE="base"
# Daytona (SANDBOX_PROVIDER=daytona)
#DAYTONA_API_KEY=""
#DAYTONA_API_URL="https://app.daytona.io/api"
#DAYTONA_SNAPSHOT=""

# --- Phase 9 (sites): opt-in real-API smoke tests (scripts/live/*.mts) ---
# Read ONLY by `npx tsx scripts/live/run-all.mts` and the manual
# .github/workflows/live-smoke.yml job — never by the app and never in normal
# CI. Each provider SKIPS unless its keys are set. Use scratch accounts and
# projects. Hosting tokens for the app itself are entered per connection in
# Sites → Hosting (encrypted at rest), not here.
#LIVE_ONLY=""                     # e.g. "netlify,anthropic"; empty = all
#LIVE_DEPLOY_WRITE=""             # "1" = also deploy + roll back (creates deployments)
#LIVE_GITHUB_TOKEN=""
#LIVE_GITHUB_REPO=""              # owner/name
#LIVE_GITHUB_BRANCH="main"
#LIVE_WORDPRESS_URL=""
#LIVE_WORDPRESS_USER=""
#LIVE_WORDPRESS_APP_PASSWORD=""
#LIVE_WEBFLOW_TOKEN=""
#LIVE_WEBFLOW_SITE_ID=""
#LIVE_VERCEL_TOKEN=""
#LIVE_VERCEL_TEAM_ID=""
#LIVE_VERCEL_PROJECT=""
#LIVE_CLOUDFLARE_TOKEN=""
#LIVE_CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=""
#LIVE_CLOUDFLARE_PROJECT=""
#LIVE_NETLIFY_TOKEN=""
#LIVE_NETLIFY_SITE_ID=""
#LIVE_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=""
#LIVE_ANTHROPIC_MODEL="claude-opus-5-5"

# --- Phase 11 (conncore): connector apps ---
# Microsoft identity platform app (Azure "App registrations", multi-tenant +
# personal accounts) for the Outlook mail and Outlook calendar connectors.
# Redirect URIs: <app>/api/connectors/outlook/callback and
# <app>/api/connectors/outlook-calendar/callback. Delegated Graph permissions:
# User.Read, Mail.Read, Mail.Send, Calendars.ReadWrite, offline_access.
#MICROSOFT_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=""
#MICROSOFT_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=""
# Slack app (Slack "Create app" → OAuth & Permissions, redirect URL
# <app>/api/connectors/slack/callback; Event Subscriptions
# request URL: <app>/api/hooks/slack/events, bot events app_mention +
# message.im). Without SLACK_SIGNING_SECRET the events receiver answers 503.
#SLACK_CLIENT_ID=""
#SLACK_CLIENT_SECRET=""
#SLACK_SIGNING_SECRET=""
# HubSpot public app (CRM sync). Redirect URI: <app>/api/connectors/hubspot/callback.
#HUBSPOT_CLIENT_ID=""
#HUBSPOT_CLIENT_SECRET=""
# --- Phase 11 (devtools): work-tool connector apps ---
# Linear OAuth2 application (Linear Settings → API → OAuth applications).
# Callback URL: <app>/api/connectors/linear/callback.
#LINEAR_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=""
#LINEAR_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=""
# Atlassian OAuth 2.0 (3LO) app for Jira Cloud (developer.atlassian.com →
# Developer console → Authorization: OAuth 2.0; Permissions: Jira API with
# read:jira-work, write:jira-work, read:jira-user). Callback URL:
# <app>/api/connectors/jira/callback.
#ATLASSIAN_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=""
#ATLASSIAN_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=""
# Airtable OAuth integration (airtable.com/create/oauth; generate a client
# secret; scopes data.records:read, data.records:write, schema.bases:read).
# Redirect URL: <app>/api/connectors/airtable/callback. PKCE is automatic.
#AIRTABLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=""
#AIRTABLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=""
# --- Phase 11 (seotools) ---
# Core Web Vitals via the PageSpeed Insights API (live site audits). Optional:
# keyless calls work at a low shared quota; a key raises it.
PAGESPEED_API_KEY=""
# Phase 14 (connectors): a merchant connects THEIR OWN store with no env vars
# at all — Settings → Connectors → Shopify → "Dev Dashboard app" (client ID +
# secret of an app in the store's own Shopify organization; ShapesOS requests
# 24-hour tokens with the client credentials grant) or "Existing custom app
# token". The variables below are only for a hosted ShapesOS Shopify app
# installed per store with OAuth.
# Phase 11 (bizsync): Shopify app (Partners → Apps → your app). Allowed
# redirect URL: <app>/api/connectors/shopify/callback. App webhooks are signed
# with the client secret and delivered to the existing signed ingest route
# <app>/api/substrate/graph/webhooks/shopify?workspaceId=… (registered by the
# shopify.register_webhooks tool; needs APP_URL). SHOPIFY_API_VERSION pins the
# Admin GraphQL version (default 2026-07).
#SHOPIFY_CLIENT_ID=""
#SHOPIFY_CLIENT_SECRET=""
#SHOPIFY_API_VERSION="2026-07"
# Phase 11 (bizsync): QuickBooks Online app (developer.intuit.com → your app →
# Keys & credentials). Redirect URI: <app>/api/connectors/quickbooks/callback.
# QUICKBOOKS_ENVIRONMENT=sandbox uses Intuit's sandbox API host (default production).
#QUICKBOOKS_CLIENT_ID=""
#QUICKBOOKS_CLIENT_SECRET=""
#QUICKBOOKS_ENVIRONMENT="production"
# Phase 11 (bizsync): Xero app (developer.xero.com → My Apps, web app). Redirect
# URI: <app>/api/connectors/xero/callback. Scopes: offline_access
# accounting.invoices accounting.payments accounting.manualjournals
# accounting.contacts accounting.settings.read. The organisation is picked in
# Settings → Connectors → Business sync after connecting.
#XERO_CLIENT_ID=""
#XERO_CLIENT_SECRET=""
# Phase 14 (connectors): Gusto payroll (dev.gusto.com → Applications). Redirect
# URI: <app>/api/connectors/gusto/callback. GUSTO_ENVIRONMENT=production uses
# api.gusto.com; anything else (default) uses the demo host api.gusto-demo.com,
# so nothing real is paid until you switch deliberately. Gusto assigns the
# app's scopes during review: ask for employees:read, payrolls:read and
# payrolls:write. GUSTO_API_VERSION pins X-Gusto-API-Version (default 2026-06-15).
#GUSTO_CLIENT_ID=""
#GUSTO_CLIENT_SECRET=""
#GUSTO_ENVIRONMENT="demo"
#GUSTO_API_VERSION="2026-06-15"

# --- Phase 12 (mfgpos) ---
# Point of sale: card payments use Stripe Terminal through each workspace's OWN
# Stripe key (Finance settings) and the register's reader id (tmr_…).
# POS_TERMINAL_MOCK=1 swaps in a labelled MOCK terminal that approves every
# card payment without a reader — for demos and tests only; such payments are
# recorded as provider "stripe_terminal_mock", never as real card money.
#POS_TERMINAL_MOCK="0"

# --- Phase 15.1 (keys): every key the code reads, by source (docs/KEYS.md) ---
# Context.dev platform key ("Both"): used when a workspace hasn't connected its
# own Context.dev key; charged 1 credit per Context.dev credit
# (lib/knowledge/contextdev/keys.ts). Leave empty to require each workspace's own.
#CONTEXTDEV_API_KEY=""
# Twilio (platform): SMS, call tracking, voice minutes, numbers, transcription
# — metered in credits (lib/calls/billing.ts). API key + secret are an
# alternative to the auth token for REST calls.
#TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=""
#TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=""
#TWILIO_API_KEY=""
#TWILIO_API_SECRET=""
# Prospect enrichment providers (platform): ordered chain, "fake" by default
# (lib/enrichment/provider.ts), e.g. "apollo,hunter".
#ENRICHMENT_PROVIDERS="fake"
#APOLLO_API_KEY=""
#HUNTER_API_KEY=""
# LiveKit voice (platform). VOICE_LIVEKIT_MODE=rehearsal (default) |
# self-hosted (LIVEKIT_URL/_API_KEY/_API_SECRET) | cloud (LIVEKIT_CLOUD_*).
#VOICE_LIVEKIT_MODE="rehearsal"
#LIVEKIT_URL=""
#LIVEKIT_API_KEY=""
#LIVEKIT_API_SECRET=""
#LIVEKIT_CLOUD_URL=""
#LIVEKIT_CLOUD_API_KEY=""
#LIVEKIT_CLOUD_API_SECRET=""
# OAuth apps (Connect): each workspace authorises its own account.
#NOTION_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=""
#NOTION_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=""
#WEBFLOW_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=""
#WEBFLOW_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=""
#BUFFER_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=""
#BUFFER_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=""
# Documenso webhook signing secret (X-Documenso-Secret). A host setting even
# when a hosted workspace connects its own Documenso (Settings → Providers).
#DOCUMENSO_WEBHOOK_SECRET=""
# Vibe CTV (BYOK media buying; lib/flywheel/ctv/vibe.ts). VIBE_TEST_MODE=1
# keeps every call in Vibe's test mode.
#VIBE_CLIENT_ID=""
#VIBE_CLIENT_SECRET=""
#VIBE_API_TOKEN=""
#VIBE_TEST_MODE="1"
# Media buying safety rails (lib/media/safety.ts): spend above this needs a
# second person; approved buys must execute within the window.
#MEDIA_TWO_PERSON_THRESHOLD_CENTS="100000"
#MEDIA_EXECUTION_WINDOW_HOURS="72"
# Local Data Exchange prototype (listings) behind a feature flag.
#MARKETR_LDE_PROTOTYPE="0"
# Not host settings (set by ShapesOS INSIDE a sandbox, never on the host):
# SHAPES_GIT_TOKEN, OUTPUT_DIR and the egress gateway's ALLOW / ALLOW_PORTS /
# EGRESS_PORT / GATEWAY_TOKEN / PREVIEW_PORT / SANDBOX_HOST /
# EXIT_WHEN_SANDBOX_GONE.

# --- Phase 15.4 (zernio) — LIVE / pre-added platform key ---
# Zernio (zernio.com, docs.zernio.com): ads on Meta, Google, TikTok, LinkedIn,
# Pinterest, X and OpenAI, and social publishing on 16 platforms, through ONE
# platform key. Every workspace gets its own Zernio profile on first use;
# customers connect their accounts per platform in Settings → Connectors →
# Zernio (no key for them to paste). On hosted (DEPLOYMENT_MODE=hosted) Zernio
# is the default social publisher when this is set. Unset: production says
# "Zernio is not connected"; dev/tests run the labelled FAKE Zernio (MOCK).
# Creating ads and raising budgets always ask (Tier 3). Connected accounts
# beyond the plan's included ones are metered monthly (zernio_account_month,
# /api/cron/zernio-accounts). The free tier (2 accounts) is enough for a live smoke.
#ZERNIO_API_KEY=""
# Base URL override (default https://zernio.com/api; paths are /v1/…).
#ZERNIO_BASE_URL=""

# --- Deploy PR (WS=state): several instances, no shared disk ---
# Production runs 2+ web replicas plus a worker with NO shared disk. Set
# MARKETR_STORAGE="s3" (with the MARKETR_S3_* settings above — Cloudflare R2,
# MinIO or AWS S3) and every file the app keeps — uploads, run recordings,
# report PDFs, briefs, logos, site working copies, fix snapshots, sitemaps,
# the published knowledge corpus — goes to the bucket (blob layer:
# lib/filesystem/storage.ts; inventory: lib/filesystem/STORAGE.md). With
# "local" each kind keeps its historic directory (the *_STORAGE_DIR settings
# above); files the app did not create under a known namespace go here:
#MARKETR_BLOB_DIR="./.data/blobs"
# On AWS the S3 client also takes the default credential chain when
# MARKETR_S3_ACCESS_KEY / _SECRET_KEY are empty: these env keys, or the ECS /
# Fargate task role (AWS sets the container URI itself; EC2 instance metadata
# and SSO profiles are not supported).
#AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=""
#AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=""
#AWS_SESSION_TOKEN=""
#AWS_CONTAINER_CREDENTIALS_RELATIVE_URI=""
#AWS_CONTAINER_CREDENTIALS_FULL_URI=""
#AWS_CONTAINER_AUTHORIZATION_TOKEN=""
# Graceful shutdown (lib/runtime/shutdown.ts, web and worker): on SIGTERM the
# instance answers /api/health with 503 "draining", open SSE streams send
# `event: reconnect` (the browser resumes on another replica), agent work is
# handed to the queue, and the process exits within SHUTDOWN_GRACE_MS. Keep it
# under the platform's stop timeout (Render and ECS default to 30 s).
#SHUTDOWN_GRACE_MS="25000"
# How long running agent jobs / inline chat turns may finish before they are
# handed back to the queue (their transcript is saved; another worker resumes).
#SHUTDOWN_HANDOFF_MS="8000"
# Node keep-alive for the Next standalone server (read by .next/standalone
# server.js): keep it ABOVE the load balancer's idle timeout (AWS ALB: 300 s)
# so the LB never reuses a socket Node already closed. SSE streams also send a
# ": ping" every 15 s (Cloudflare drops idle connections at ~100 s, CloudFront
# wants a byte every 30 s).
#KEEP_ALIVE_TIMEOUT="310000"
# Two-instance smoke (scripts/smoke/multi-instance.mts; needs `npm run build`
# first). DATABASE_URL = schema owner (seeding); the replicas and worker run as
# SMOKE_APP_DATABASE_URL (default DATABASE_URL). The admin sign-in uses
# E2E_ADMIN_EMAIL / E2E_ADMIN_PASSWORD. SMOKE_REAL_S3=1 uses your MARKETR_S3_*
# bucket instead of the in-process fake.
#SMOKE_APP_DATABASE_URL=""
#E2E_ADMIN_PASSWORD=""
#SMOKE_PORT_A="3101"
#SMOKE_PORT_B="3102"
#SMOKE_GRACE_MS="20000"
#SMOKE_REAL_S3=""
#SMOKE_SKIP_WORKER=""
# --- Deploy PR (infra): website and OS on two hostnames (proxy.ts,
# lib/hosting/host-routing.ts) ---
# When BOTH are set (and differ), WEBSITE_HOST serves the public website (the
# landing page, /pricing; later /legal, /docs, /download) and APP_HOST serves
# the OS (dashboard, sign-in, portal, CMS admin, API). A page requested on the
# wrong host gets a redirect (308; "/" on the app host → /dashboard, 307).
# /api/*, auth and OAuth callbacks, /mcp, assets and the public share pages
# (/r, /s, /book, /events, /shop) are never redirected, and any other host
# (tenant custom domains, domains.shapesos.com) is never touched. Unset =
# today's behaviour (self-host, dev, CI, e2e). Register OAuth callbacks on the
# app host, and set NEXTAUTH_URL / AUTH_URL / APP_URL to the app host's URL
# (e.g. https://app.shapesos.com). Bare host names, optional :port.
#WEBSITE_HOST="shapesos.com"
#APP_HOST="app.shapesos.com"
# Hosted start wrapper (scripts/deploy/with-runtime-env.sh; render.yaml and
# infra/aws): when DATABASE_URL is unset, it is composed from these plus
# APP_DB_USER / APP_DB_PASSWORD (above), so the app connects as the
# least-privilege role while the platform only hands out the owner's URL.
# SHAPESOS_DB_OWNER_* are for the AWS migrate task only (--owner). On AWS,
# each SHAPESOS_ENV_JSON_* holds a whole Secrets Manager secret (a JSON object
# of KEY: value); its non-empty keys are exported unless already set. Unused
# under compose.
#SHAPESOS_DB_HOST=""
#SHAPESOS_DB_PORT="5432"
#SHAPESOS_DB_NAME=""
#SHAPESOS_DB_OWNER_USER=""
#SHAPESOS_DB_OWNER_PASSWORD=""
#SHAPESOS_ENV_JSON_SHARED=""
#SHAPESOS_ENV_JSON_WEB=""
#SHAPESOS_ENV_JSON_WORKER=""
# Backups on Render (scripts/ops/backup.sh; docs/ops/BACKUP-RESTORE.md):
# BACKUP_SOURCE=render-export copies Render's own logical export to the
# BACKUP_S3_* bucket instead of running pg_dump (Render's owner user can't
# dump FORCE-RLS tables). Needs a Render API key and the database id (dpg-…).
#BACKUP_SOURCE="pg_dump"
#RENDER_API_KEY=""
#RENDER_POSTGRES_ID=""
#BACKUP_EXPORT_TIMEOUT_SECONDS="3600"
#BACKUP_EXPORT_POLL_SECONDS="15"
# Tests only: point backup.sh at a fake Render API.
#RENDER_API_BASE=""

# --- Phase 17: latency ---
# Connection pool of THIS process (Prisma connection_limit), applied when
# DATABASE_URL carries none. Unset = Prisma's default (num_cpus × 2 + 1).
# Keep (web replicas + workers) × pool under the database's limit; behind
# PgBouncer (transaction mode) see docs/deploy/RENDER.md §6 "Connections".
#DATABASE_POOL_SIZE="10"
# Warm the local recall embedder (MiniLM) in the background at boot so the
# first chat turn doesn't pay the model load. 0 = load on first use.
#MEMORY_WARM_AT_BOOT="1"
# The latency battery (scripts/verify/latency.mts; fake model, never paid):
# samples per measure, budget slack (×3 default; STRICT=1 → ×1), ASSERT=0
# only reports, BASE_URL targets a running app instead of starting one,
# PORT / DEV=1 (next dev even when a build exists) / LOG_DIR for the app it
# starts, APP_DATABASE_URL = the least-privilege role the app runs as.
#LATENCY_RUNS="20"
#LATENCY_SLACK="3"
#LATENCY_STRICT=""
#LATENCY_ASSERT="1"
#LATENCY_BASE_URL=""
#LATENCY_PORT="3117"
#LATENCY_DEV=""
#LATENCY_LOG_DIR=""
#LATENCY_APP_DATABASE_URL=""

# ── Phase 18.1: Spotlight (⌘K search, lib/search) ─────────────────────────
# Meaning-search embeds the query with the local MiniLM model (the same one
# Growth Memory uses, cached under MEMORY_MODEL_CACHE). "off" keeps Spotlight
# to name + full-text matches (e.g. a small box without the model).
# SPOTLIGHT_SEMANTIC=on
# Index the text inside each uploaded file / saved Office doc right away
# (in the background). "off" leaves it to the search-index cron and
# scripts/search/backfill-text-index.mts.
# SPOTLIGHT_INDEX_ON_WRITE=on
# Records the /api/cron/search-index sweep (re)indexes per run (default 200).
# SEARCH_INDEX_BATCH=200

# ── Phase 18.2 (WS=content): live collaboration (Notes co-editing) ─────────
# The browser connects to the collab server (lib/collab/server.ts,
# @hocuspocus/server) at COLLAB_PUBLIC_URL with a 5-minute token the app
# mints (/api/collab/token, signed with AUTH_SECRET). Unset = notes save
# without live co-editing. Run ONE collab process: the worker starts it when
# COLLAB_PORT is set (local + docker compose); on Render it is the
# single-instance shapesos-collab web service (scripts/collab.mts, which
# listens on COLLAB_PORT, else PORT).
# COLLAB_PUBLIC_URL=ws://localhost:1235
# COLLAB_PORT=1235

# ── Phase 18.3 (WS=flow): Web Push (browser notifications) ──────────────────
# VAPID keys (RFC 8292) sign every push; messages are encrypted per browser
# (RFC 8291, aes128gcm) with node:crypto — no web-push package. Unset = Web
# Push is off and Settings says why (nothing is faked). Generate a pair with:
#   npx tsx -e 'import("./lib/push/vapid").then(m=>console.log(m.generateVapidKeys()))'
# VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=   (65-byte uncompressed P-256 point, base64url)
# VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=  (32-byte P-256 key, base64url — a secret)
# VAPID_SUBJECT=mailto:ops@example.com   (or an https: URL the push service can reach you at)
# Only the browser push services are contacted (FCM, Mozilla, Windows, Apple).
# Comma-separated extra hosts for a self-hosted push service (rare):
# WEB_PUSH_EXTRA_HOSTS=

# ── Phase 18.3 (WS=flow): Time Machine (workspace snapshots) ────────────────
# Snapshots go to the blob store's "snapshots" namespace (S3 with
# MARKETR_STORAGE=s3). With MARKETR_STORAGE=local they live here (default
# .data/blobs/snapshots); production needs durable storage (see STORAGE.md).
# SNAPSHOT_STORAGE_DIR="/var/lib/marketr/snapshots"
# Largest snapshot kept / restored, compressed MB (default 256).
# SNAPSHOT_MAX_MB=256

# ── Phase 19B (WS=engine): Dress Rehearsal — town layouts from Figma ────────
# A Figma personal access token (file read scope) used ONLY to import a town
# layout frame for Dress Rehearsal (lib/sim/figma.ts: GET /v1/files/:key/nodes).
# Not a general Figma connector. Unset = "Import from Figma" says why; the
# procedural town generator always works.
# FIGMA_TOKEN=""

# ── Phase 19B (WS=panel): Dress Rehearsal — the Pre Launch Panel ────────────
# Pro and above (entitlement dress_rehearsal). Model calls go through the
# router's "copy" workload (LLM_MODEL_COPY; Anthropic / OpenAI keys above),
# metered, under each run's confirmed hard credit cap. Screenshots and traces
# go to the blob store's "rehearsal" namespace.
# Personas of one run walking at the same time (1–6, default 3; never more
# than MARKETR_MAX_BROWSER_RECORDINGS browsers on this process).
# PANEL_MAX_PARALLEL_PERSONAS=3
# TESTS AND LOCAL SMOKE ONLY: "1" swaps the model for a deterministic FAKE
# model (labelled "Fake model" on every report; nothing is called or charged).
# Refused when NODE_ENV=production.
# PANEL_FAKE_MODEL=
